quran[10]{c,v,t}:
  58,12,"O believers! When you consult the Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) privately, offer some charity (to the needy) before your private consultation. That is better for you and purer. But if you do not find (anything to give in charity), then Allah is surely Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful."
  58,13,"Are you worried about charitable offerings before you come to speak privately (with the Messenger [blessings and peace be upon him])? Since you could not do it, Allah has mercifully turned to you. So establish the prayer, pay the alms due and obey Allah and His Messenger ([blessings and peace be upon him] persistently). And Allah is All-Aware of what you do."
  58,14,Have you not seen those who become intimate friends with a people with whom Allah is wrathful? They are neither from you nor (are you) from them. And they knowingly swear false oaths (claiming to be with you).
  58,15,Allah has prepared a severe punishment for them. Evil indeed is what they used to do.
  58,16,"They take their (false) oaths as a shield and bar (others) from the way of Allah. So, there shall be a humiliating punishment for them."
  58,17,"Neither their properties nor their children will avail them against Allah in the least. They shall be the inmates of the Fire, and they shall remain in it forever."
  58,18,"The Day Allah resurrects them all together, they will swear to Him, just like they swear to you (now), supposing they have some standing. Beware! They are indeed liars!"
  58,19,"Satan has gained control over them and has caused them to forget the remembrance of Allah. They are the party of Satan. Know! Indeed, it is the party of Satan who are the losers."
  58,20,"Indeed, those who oppose Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) will be among the most abased."
  58,21,"Allah has decreed: ‘I and My messengers will surely prevail.’ Indeed, Allah is All-Strong, All-Mighty."
